   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">I&#39;m working on a Shiny server that processes large datasets and emails results. We&#39;ve written code to compute and mail the results, but we would like to implement a queuing system to process each submission in the order received.</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">I plan on utilizing the Queue class described here: <a href=\"http://www.r-bloggers.com/implementing-a-queue-as-a-reference-class/\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(0,89,153)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.r-bloggers.com/implementing-a-queue-as-a-reference-class/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393356714000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1yhTBXO3n4MuP2AC8SkkvT\">http://www.r-bloggers.com/implementing-a-queue-as-a-reference-class/</a></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><strong><br></strong></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><strong>Currently</strong> our flow works like this:</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:19.5px\">1. </span><span style=\"line-height:17px\">A person will input a CSV file and their email into our shiny app.</span></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:17px\">2. The startServer file observes the submit button, and makes calls to a plotting method (in plotting.R), which plots the data as a PNG, and returns the filename.</span></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:17px\">3. The returned filename and email are then passed by shinyServer to the mailing method (in mail.R) which mails out the data.</span></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">Note: the calls to mail and plotting are not set as &quot;local=TRUE&quot;, thus they are in the global environment.</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><strong>My idea</strong> is to:</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:19.5px\">1. </span><span style=\"line-height:17px\">Declare a Queue object (q) outside of the startServer method but still in server.R and call q$push(inputtedData, email).</span></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:17px\">2. From there, the queue object would make the calls to compute and mail the file to the client, and wait until each job is done before moving onto the next.</span></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:17px\"><br></span></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><strong>The problem</strong> is that I&#39;m not sure how to allow the Queue file to accept asynchronous calls to push new data onto the queue structure. Seeing as startServer is a per-session environment, what must I consider as I implement a shared queue.</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">Links that I am using for reference:</p><p style=\"clear:both\"><font color=\"#242729\" face=\"Arial, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px;line-height:19.5px\">Asynchronous calls <a href=\"https://www.rforge.net/doc/packages/background/async.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.rforge.net/doc/packages/background/async.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393356714000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Jx6UWeVGWDMiRWudiscsx\">https://www.rforge.net/doc/packages/background/async.html</a></span></font></p><p style=\"clear:both\"><font color=\"#242729\" face=\"Arial, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px;line-height:19.5px\">Scoping in R shiny <a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/scoping.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/scoping.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393356714000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0TZMsYMEZy7P4l7vnk6o7r\">http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/scoping.html</a></span></font></p><p style=\"clear:both\"><font color=\"#242729\" face=\"Arial, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px;line-height:19.5px\">Parallel package <a href=\"https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/parallel/doc/parallel.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/parallel/doc/parallel.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393356714000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0HKi93lvzZYWN69x3mMoq2\">https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/parallel/doc/parallel.pdf</a></span></font></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">Thanks in advance, and please let me know if I missed anything.</p></div>"
